    "title": "Is Bill Murray rooting for UConn in March Madness?",
    "text": "NCAABIs Bill Murray rooting for UConn in March Madness?Wajih AlBaroudiFor The WinMarch 20, 2026, 2:02 p.m. ETKeep WatchingBill Murray is a hard person to track down.The legendary actor famously does not have an agent nor a publicist, so he uses a 1-800 number and voicemail system to hear from friends and colleagues.So, if you don't have that number, the next best spot to meet Murray might be a UConn men's basketball game. Why, you may ask? You've come to the right place.Is Bill Murray a UConn fan?By association, yes!Murray's son, Luke Murray, has been an assistant coach under Dan Hurley since 2021, winning consecutive championships in 2023 and '24. Bill, 75, has regularly attended games during that time and even celebrated on court with the Huskies' after their national title wins.So, it would not be surprising at all to see Bill cheering on the Huskies as March Madness continues. We'll be on the lookout.Average Cost To Rent A Private Jet For Seniors! (Take A Look)QuickSearches | Private Jet Rental | SponsoredSponsoredLearn MoreUndoBrain Fog Has Been Linked to This Common Daily Food. Did You Eat It?plusvitalhealthy | SponsoredSponsoredLearn MoreUndoNAD+ Is The Ozempic Of Anti-Aging (Buy It Now)Direct Meds NAD+ | SponsoredSponsoredLearn MoreUndoMobile Protection Trailers Have Gotten Everyone Talking About Them! (Take A Look)QuickSearches | mobile protection trailers | SponsoredSponsoredLearn MoreUndoby Taboolaby TaboolaWould you like to know more?- | SponsoredSponsoredUndoIf You're Collecting Under $3950 In SS a Month: You're Eligible for These 10 DiscountsSilverPenny | SponsoredSponsoredLearn moreUndoStiff Rotator Cuff? This 12-Minute Method Relieves The AcheShoulder Relief News | SponsoredSponsoredUndoUltra-Soft Linen Shorts Loved by Thousands of MenWalkergrey | SponsoredSponsoredShop NowUndoPlastic Surgeons Reveal: Forget Collagen, Use This Household Item InsteadAnti-Aging Center | SponsoredSponsoredRead MoreUndoby Taboolaby TaboolaThis may be of inte